<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>If you're looking for ranch entrance gates in Waco, TX, you've probably driven past a hundred entrances and noticed the difference between the ones done right and the ones sagging off a bent T-post. A proper entrance starts with heavy steel, deep concrete footings, and posts sized for the gate they carry. Brazos Ridge Fence Co. builds custom entrances across McLennan, Bosque, and Falls counties, from a clean 16-foot steel swing gate to a full limestone-column entrance with an overhead arch and your ranch name cut in steel.</p><p>Most of our custom entrances run $5,000 to $25,000 and up depending on gate width, stonework, and automation. We also install cattle guards, automatic gate operators, and solar power setups for entrances a mile off the nearest meter. Every job starts with a free written estimate, and every price is in writing before we dig the first hole. Call us at (509) 351-8404 and we'll come walk your entrance with you.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Custom Steel Swing Gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Heavy-wall steel frames from 12 to 24 feet wide, welded on site or in our shop and hung on posts set in concrete. No sag, no drag, no chain holding it shut.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Limestone and Rock Columns</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Native Texas limestone or ledgestone columns built on real footings, sized to match your gate. They anchor the whole entrance and never need paint.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Automatic Gate Operators</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Open the gate from your truck with a remote, keypad, or your phone. We install commercial-grade operators rated for heavy steel gates and daily ranch traffic.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Cattle Guards Installed</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Load-rated steel cattle guards set on concrete foundations, installed for $3,500 to $8,000 depending on width and rating. Drive through without stopping while your cattle stay put.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Overhead Arches and Ranch Signs</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Steel arches with your ranch name, brand, or established date cut by plasma. It's the detail people remember about your place.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Solar Power for Remote Entrances</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">No power at the road? A solar panel and battery bank will run an automatic operator year-round, even through a cloudy Central Texas January.</p>
      </div>
</div>
